This directory is Lua 5.4.7's core source (lapi.c, lauxlib.c, lstate.c,
etc.), vendored verbatim -- including luauser.c, a UE4SS-specific
addition, not part of stock Lua -- from:

    https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/tree/main/deps/first/LuaRaw

Vendored (rather than linked against UE4SS.dll) because UE4SS.dll does
not export the Lua C API -- confirmed via `dumpbin /exports` against a
real installed build. See dev-notes/progress.md's "Transport flip" entry
for why this is safe: this module statically links its own copy of the
exact same source UE4SS itself compiles, so the two independently-built
copies agree on lua_State's internal layout when sharing the same
pointer.

